    {
      "id": "emergent_municipal_governance_network",
      "description": "A coalition of public-sector AI ethics officers and municipal IT directors, disillusioned by top-down mandates and punitive enforcement, forms a transnational network to share compliant yet locally adaptive AI governance templates. Sparked by Florence task force discussions and fueled by backlash against the Cohesion Fund penalties, the network begins publishing interoperable safety overrides and human-in-the-loop blueprints. It is not an official body, but it starts filling the vacuum left by fragmented EU implementation.",
      "first_turn": 12,
